Backport of upstream pygfx PR #1329 (open at the time of writing):
"Make the generated WGSL comply with the spec"

    https://github.com/pygfx/pygfx/pull/1329

Fixes three constructs that naga accepts but that are invalid WGSL, and that
Tint (Dawn's WGSL compiler) rejects at shader creation:

- Integral user-defined vertex outputs must use flat interpolation; the
  Varyings struct now adds @interpolate(flat) to i32/u32 varyings.
- A const-expression evaluating to NaN is a shader-creation error; the NaN for
  degenerate line vertices is now computed from a var at runtime.
- Bitwise and arithmetic operators cannot be mixed without parentheses; two
  expressions in noise.wgsl are parenthesized as naga already parsed them.

The upstream commit also adds a test; only the pygfx/ hunks are backported here.

diff --git a/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/shader/resolve.py b/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/shader/resolve.py
index bd9b7f37b..432e2afb7 100644
--- a/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/shader/resolve.py
+++ b/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/shader/resolve.py
@@ -234,7 +234,14 @@ def update_lines(self, lines):
             # Build struct
             struct_lines = ["struct Varyings {"]
             for slotnr, name in enumerate(used_slots):
-                struct_lines.append(f"    @location({slotnr}) {name} : {types[name]},")
+                # WGSL requires integral user-defined vertex outputs to use flat interpolation
+                type = types[name]
+                interpolate = (
+                    " @interpolate(flat)" if "i32" in type or "u32" in type else ""
+                )
+                struct_lines.append(
+                    f"    @location({slotnr}){interpolate} {name} : {type},"
+                )
             for name in sorted(used_builtins):
                 struct_lines.append(f"    @builtin({name}) {name} : {types[name]},")
             struct_lines.append("};\n")
